even in death I'm funny.

251
00:12:08,348 --> 00:12:09,328
- Who is it?

252
00:12:09,328 --> 00:12:10,352
- It's me Sandy.

253
00:12:10,352 --> 00:12:11,440
- [Voiceover] You're little conscience.

254
00:12:11,440 --> 00:12:12,699
- Sandy.

255
00:12:12,699 --> 00:12:13,829
- What are you doing?

256
00:12:13,829 --> 00:12:15,781
- Sandy look, do me a favor will you

257
00:12:15,781 --> 00:12:18,736
and run out and play somewhere, I'm busy.

258
00:12:18,736 --> 00:12:23,557
- [Voiceover] Oh, I see another
corpse turned into seaweed.

259
00:12:23,557 --> 00:12:25,724
(singing)

260
00:12:27,813 --> 00:12:29,616
- Don't you like me anymore?

261
00:12:29,616 --> 00:12:30,896
- [Voiceover] Well you're
assuming I liked you in

262
00:12:30,896 --> 00:12:31,729
the first place.

263
00:12:31,729 --> 00:12:33,200
- Sure I like you, I love you.

264
00:12:33,200 --> 00:12:36,102
I just want to be by myself.

265
00:12:36,102 --> 00:12:37,701
- Where were you last night?

266
00:12:37,701 --> 00:12:38,908
- [Voiceover] Oh, killing someone...

267
00:12:38,908 --> 00:12:42,256
- We had a beach barbeque
and everyone on the island

268
00:12:42,256 --> 00:12:43,323
was there.

269
00:12:43,323 --> 00:12:44,293
- [Voiceover] Except half.

270
00:12:44,293 --> 00:12:46,384
- Ned was looking all over for you.

271
00:12:46,384 --> 00:12:48,261
- Sandy, please run along.

272
00:12:48,261 --> 00:12:50,678
- Okay, sorry to disturb you.

273
00:12:52,933 --> 00:12:56,347
I almost forgot, the
wedding announcements came

274
00:12:56,347 --> 00:12:58,000
and mommy wants you to look at one before

275
00:12:58,000 --> 00:12:59,131
we send them out.

276
00:12:59,131 --> 00:13:01,413
There's only a week til the big day.

277
00:13:01,413 --> 00:13:02,496
- Okay, okay.

278
00:13:04,517 --> 00:13:05,684
- What's that?

279
00:13:09,936 --> 00:13:11,024
Look what I found?

280
00:13:11,024 --> 00:13:15,205
- [Voiceover] I think
it's a piece of brain.

281
00:13:15,205 --> 00:13:18,288
- [Voiceover] Gilligan, give me that.

282
00:13:19,292 --> 00:13:21,381
- [Voiceover] And it's still
ticking, I'm John Cameron

283
00:13:21,381 --> 00:13:22,881
Swayzee for Timex.

284
00:13:26,410 --> 00:13:28,699
- No, I'll take care of it.

285
00:13:28,699 --> 00:13:30,492
- [Voiceover] Oh, geez, Haley
Mills gets the Parent Trap,

286
00:13:30,492 --> 00:13:32,783
I get stuck in the lousy...

287
00:13:32,783 --> 00:13:35,366
(upbeat music)

288
00:13:39,789 --> 00:13:42,266
- I'd better take it easy.

289
00:13:42,266 --> 00:13:46,351
I didn't find any dead
woman, only seaweed.

290
00:13:46,351 --> 00:13:48,399
I know what's the matter
with me, I'm seeing things.

291
00:13:48,399 --> 00:13:50,394
I'm letting my imagination run wild.

292
00:13:50,394 --> 00:13:51,535
- [Voiceover] You're also doing voiceovers

293
00:13:51,535 --> 00:13:52,644
for crappy movies.

294
00:13:52,644 --> 00:13:55,066
- Why should it bother me?

295
00:13:55,066 --> 00:13:58,202
I didn't do anything to
Vi, I didn't kill her.

296
00:13:58,202 --> 00:13:59,588
It's her own fault she's dead.

297
00:13:59,588 --> 00:14:03,023
- [Voiceover] It's her own
fault I didn't save her.

298
00:14:03,023 --> 00:14:04,911
- [Voiceover] I love
myself unconditionally,

299
00:14:04,911 --> 00:14:07,621
I love myself
unconditionally, I love myself

300
00:14:07,621 --> 00:14:08,922
unconditionally.

301
00:14:08,922 --> 00:14:11,172
(groaning)

302
00:14:13,658 --> 00:14:16,708
- [Voiceover] I need a
vacation, something urban,

303
00:14:16,708 --> 00:14:19,125
the Quad Cities or Davenport.

304
00:14:21,252 --> 00:14:22,458
- [Voiceover] Think I'll
return to the scene of

305
00:14:22,458 --> 00:14:24,875
the crime to cheer myself up.

306
00:14:26,084 --> 00:14:26,917
It worked.

307
00:14:29,029 --> 00:14:33,196
- [Voiceover] Honey, I'm
home, oh yeah, you're dead.

308
00:14:34,138 --> 00:14:38,305
- [Voiceover] (singing) The
long and winding stairs.

309
00:14:40,996 --> 00:14:42,596
- [Voiceover] Boy you
know, a pair of pants

310
00:14:42,596 --> 00:14:45,679
would feel real good right about now.

311
00:14:48,655 --> 00:14:50,642
- [Voiceover] I'm going
to pad out the film

312
00:14:50,642 --> 00:14:51,725
starting now.

313
00:14:55,026 --> 00:14:59,193
- [Voiceover] Oh geez, her
butt must have weighed a ton.

314
00:15:00,198 --> 00:15:04,379
- [Voiceover] Locks in place,
ready for my next victim.

315
00:15:04,379 --> 00:15:08,546
- [Voiceover] Like Colombo's
not going to figure this out.

316
00:15:09,883 --> 00:15:12,604
- [Voiceover] Now cut that out.

317
00:15:12,604 --> 00:15:14,715
- She came out here of her own accord.

318
00:15:14,715 --> 00:15:15,781
- [Voiceover] No, it was a camera.

319
00:15:15,781 --> 00:15:17,435
- It wasn't my doing she fell.

320
00:15:17,435 --> 00:15:18,821
Wasn't my fault if it gave way.

321
00:15:18,821 --> 00:15:21,776
Why should I be blamed, I
have nothing to do with it.

322
00:15:21,776 --> 00:15:23,867
Anyway, nobody ever needs to know.

323
00:15:23,867 --> 00:15:26,096
Nobody will even connect me with her.

324
00:15:26,096 --> 00:15:27,953
Why should they?

325
00:15:27,953 --> 00:15:31,173
Except for this watch of hers.

326
00:15:31,173 --> 00:15:32,006
- [Voiceover] Three skips.

327
00:15:32,006 --> 00:15:34,006
- That's the end of you.

328
00:15:36,730 --> 00:15:40,647
- [Voiceover] You're
going to die you evil man.

329
00:15:41,521 --> 00:15:44,838
- [Voiceover] I know it, I'm living it.

330
00:15:44,838 --> 00:15:47,588
- [Voiceover] Oh, I hate Mondays.

331
00:15:51,621 --> 00:15:54,683
- [Voiceover] Oh, the bridge
club will be here any minute

332
00:15:54,683 --> 00:15:56,183
and I'm not ready.

333
00:15:57,072 --> 00:15:58,428
- [Voiceover] Oh geez,
days like this I just feel

334
00:15:58,428 --> 00:16:02,595
like having a shower, a
sandwich, and straight to bed.

335
00:16:04,230 --> 00:16:07,647
- [Voiceover] Is that you Bert I. Gordon?

336
00:16:09,339 --> 00:16:12,379
- [Voiceover] Ah, my 10
o'clock, I'll be right with you.

337
00:16:12,379 --> 00:16:16,187
- [Voiceover] She's wearing today's paper.

338
00:16:16,187 --> 00:16:19,515
- [Voiceover] Meg, I
will come back to you.

339
00:16:19,515 --> 00:16:20,848
- Meg, it's you.

340
00:16:22,043 --> 00:16:23,344
- [Voiceover] This is
the greatest chick trap

341
00:16:23,344 --> 00:16:24,511
ever invented.

342
00:16:25,808 --> 00:16:29,221
- Oh no, no, it's just that
I wasn't expecting anyone.

343
00:16:29,221 --> 00:16:30,725
- [Voiceover] Anyone alive anyway.

344
00:16:30,725 --> 00:16:32,581
- What are you doing up here?

345
00:16:32,581 --> 00:16:34,081
- Looking for you.

346
00:16:35,003 --> 00:16:37,296
What are you doing up here
in this old lighthouse?

347
00:16:37,296 --> 00:16:38,597
- Well I...

348
00:16:38,597 --> 00:16:39,621
- [Voiceover] I live here.

349
00:16:39,621 --> 00:16:41,520
- I like its quiet.

350
00:16:41,520 --> 00:16:43,020
I wanted to think.

351
00:16:44,517 --> 00:16:46,288
I guess I'm worried about
that Carnegie Hall thing

352
00:16:46,288 --> 00:16:47,515
next month.

353
00:16:47,515 --> 00:16:49,020
I wonder if I'm good enough.

354
00:16:49,020 --> 00:16:51,675
- [Voiceover] Yeah, being an
usher's a big responsibility.

355
00:16:51,675 --> 00:16:53,712
- You're the best jazz
pianist in the world.

356
00:16:53,712 --> 00:16:55,173
- [Voiceover] Oh yeah,
much better than Art Tatum,

357
00:16:55,173 --> 00:16:57,090
Bud Powell, Bill Evans.

358
00:16:58,704 --> 00:17:00,837
- I never loved anyone before in my life.

359
00:17:00,837 --> 00:17:03,003
- [Voiceover] Not that survived anyway.

360
00:17:03,003 --> 00:17:04,003
- Nor did I.

361
00:17:07,131 --> 00:17:09,276
- [Voiceover] Eclipse, it's here.

362
00:17:09,276 --> 00:17:11,292
- Do you smell perfume?

363
00:17:11,292 --> 00:17:15,835
- [Voiceover] I like to
wear Chanel Number Five.

364
00:17:15,835 --> 00:17:18,407
- [Voiceover] I wanted
to smell pretty for you.

365
00:17:18,407 --> 00:17:21,564
- It's sort of cold and gloomy in here.

366
00:17:21,564 --> 00:17:23,463
I'm getting the creeps
having that big lamp

367
00:17:23,463 --> 00:17:24,530
staring at us.

368
00:17:24,530 --> 00:17:26,044
- [Voiceover] I hate the
prying eyes of furniture.

369
00:17:26,044 --> 00:17:28,178
- Locked it up here since
the light stopped working.

370
00:17:28,178 --> 00:17:30,727
Glad they're going to tear it down.

371
00:17:30,727 --> 00:17:34,770
Come on, let's go outside
til the sun's warmer.

372
00:17:34,770 --> 00:17:37,276
- [Voiceover] What a morning.

373
00:17:37,276 --> 00:17:39,858
- [Voiceover] Aye, yay, yay.

374
00:17:39,858 --> 00:17:41,000
- [Meg] Coming?

375
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:45,063
- [Voiceover] I didn't kill her, oh, oh.

376
00:17:45,063 --> 00:17:46,643
- [Voiceover] Her swimsuit
looks like it's made out

377
00:17:46,643 --> 00:17:48,310
of SNH green stamps.

378
00:17:54,003 --> 00:17:56,503
- [Voiceover] Thanks a lot Vi.

379
00:18:01,619 --> 00:18:03,036
- [Voiceover] Tonight from the crypt,

380
00:18:03,036 --> 00:18:07,203
I want to bury a lighthouse
keeper (evil laugh).

381
00:18:10,055 --> 00:18:11,955
- [Voiceover] Sessions
presents soft rock classics,

382
00:18:11,955 --> 00:18:13,160
Leo Sare.

383
00:18:13,160 --> 00:18:15,243
And Marie, and many more.

384
00:18:17,992 --> 00:18:19,452
- I'm sending the gown tomorrow.

385
00:18:19,452 --> 00:18:21,010
Oh, you're going to love it Tom.

386
00:18:21,010 --> 00:18:23,848
Oh, I was supposed to
see about a tie for dad

387
00:18:23,848 --> 00:18:25,191
and I forgot.

388
00:18:25,191 --> 00:18:28,786
I'll be so glad when this
whole thing's over with,

389
00:18:28,786 --> 00:18:30,258
won't you?

390
00:18:30,258 --> 00:18:31,719
- [Voiceover] Honey, shut up.

391
00:18:31,719 --> 00:18:33,756
- It'll only be a week more.

392
00:18:33,756 --> 00:18:35,591
We can wait that long can't we?

393
00:18:35,591 --> 00:18:39,008
- [Voiceover] No, I want to kill you now.

394
00:18:42,002 --> 00:18:44,764
- [Voiceover] Wait a minute
didn't Vi die in pumps

395
00:18:44,764 --> 00:18:47,111
and she's barefoot again.

396
00:18:47,111 --> 00:18:50,131
- [Voiceover] Honey are you
carrying a pock of Theramin?

397
00:18:50,131 --> 00:18:51,548
- I love you so much Tom.

398
00:18:51,548 --> 00:18:53,381
You love me don't you?

399
00:18:54,771 --> 00:18:56,771
- [Voiceover] My braces.

400
00:19:01,596 --> 00:19:03,541
- [Voiceover] Wait a minute,
were you just walking

401
00:19:03,541 --> 00:19:04,624
on all fours?

402
00:19:08,824 --> 00:19:11,394
- Did you see anything?

403
00:19:11,394 --> 00:19:12,514
- What there's nothing to see?

404
00:19:12,514 --> 00:19:13,998
- Right there.

405
00:19:13,998 --> 00:19:15,512
- [Voiceover] Water, source of all life.

406
00:19:15,512 --> 00:19:16,679
It's wet, why?

407
00:19:20,166 --> 00:19:22,166
- There's nothing there.

408
00:19:23,621 --> 00:19:25,297
What's been there?

409
00:19:25,297 --> 00:19:27,174
- Why you fib?

410
00:19:27,174 --> 00:19:30,174
- Babe, I've got to get out of here.

411
00:19:31,057 --> 00:19:32,005
Right away.

412
00:19:32,005 --> 00:19:33,328
- [Voiceover] I need air.

413
00:19:33,328 --> 00:19:35,952
- Let's elope, we can catch
a boat to the mainland

414
00:19:35,952 --> 00:19:38,928
and be married this afternoon.

415
00:19:38,928 --> 00:19:40,112
- What about the wedding?

416
00:19:40,112 --> 00:19:41,947
- I was never for a big deal anyway.

417
00:19:41,947 --> 00:19:44,038
I only agreed to it because you wanted it.

418
00:19:44,038 --> 00:19:45,819
- Does it matter that I still want it?

419
00:19:45,819 --> 00:19:47,611
- Please Meg, please, do this for me.

420
00:19:47,611 --> 00:19:50,331
Just go away with me right now.

421
00:19:50,331 --> 00:19:52,956
- I told you that's impossible.

422
00:19:52,956 --> 00:19:56,485
I want my mother and father
to think well of you.

423
00:19:56,485 --> 00:19:58,129
- I'll have to go by myself.

424
00:19:58,129 --> 00:19:59,099
- [Voiceover] Elope by yourself?

425
00:19:59,099 --> 00:20:01,182
- What about the wedding?

426
00:20:02,939 --> 00:20:05,509
- What about it babe?

427
00:20:05,509 --> 00:20:08,676
- If you go there won't be one though?

428
00:20:09,712 --> 00:20:10,949
- [Voiceover] Elope by himself.

429
00:20:10,949 --> 00:20:11,899
What's he going to do?

430
00:20:11,899 --> 00:20:14,649
Carry himself over the threshold?

431
00:20:15,723 --> 00:20:16,556
Men.

432
00:20:22,172 --> 00:20:23,755
- [Voiceover] Sand.

433
00:20:25,883 --> 00:20:28,016
- [Voiceover] Sessions
presents David Sole.

434
00:20:28,016 --> 00:20:29,851
- [Voiceover] (singing)
Don't give up on us babe.

435
00:20:29,851 --> 00:20:30,896
- Now I will perform the
greatest of all magic

436
00:20:30,896 --> 00:20:34,587
accomplishments ever
performed on this island.

437
00:20:34,587 --> 00:20:35,664
The secret cabinet.

438
00:20:35,664 --> 00:20:36,955
- [Voiceover] Don't you
have your own family kid?

439
00:20:36,955 --> 00:20:38,651
- The cabinet is empty.

440
00:20:38,651 --> 00:20:42,576
Tom, Tom, you're not paying any attention.

441
00:20:42,576 --> 00:20:43,717
- [Voiceover] Oh, I'm
waiting for the waitress.

442
00:20:43,717 --> 00:20:46,715
- Don't you want to
see the secret cabinet?

443
00:20:46,715 --> 00:20:49,957
- Oh sure I do, I wouldn't
miss it, go ahead.

444
00:20:49,957 --> 00:20:52,101
- If I close the doors
to this magic cabinet

445
00:20:52,101 --> 00:20:56,229
and say the magic word and
tap it with my magic wand.

446
00:20:56,229 --> 00:20:59,131
- [Voiceover] I saw her do this in Vegas,

447
00:20:59,131 --> 00:21:00,548
where's my drink?

448
00:21:02,064 --> 00:21:04,656
- It is now filled with jellybeans.

449
00:21:04,656 --> 00:21:05,656
Tom Stewart.

450
00:21:08,005 --> 00:21:09,232
- [Voiceover] Firm, huh?

451
00:21:09,232 --> 00:21:11,600
- Fine one you are.

452
00:21:11,600 --> 00:21:12,433
- Sandy.

453
00:21:13,531 --> 00:21:16,987
Sandy, if you hate me
for the rest of your life

454
00:21:16,987 --> 00:21:18,011
I deserve it.

455
00:21:18,011 --> 00:21:20,379
- I couldn't hate you
no matter what you did.

456
00:21:20,379 --> 00:21:21,424
- [Voiceover] I killed someone.

457
00:21:21,424 --> 00:21:22,608
- No matter what I did?

458
00:21:22,608 --> 00:21:23,813
- No matter what.

459
00:21:23,813 --> 00:21:25,787
- Even like fighting with your sister?

460
00:21:25,787 --> 00:21:27,344
Meg's mad at me you know.

461
00:21:27,344 --> 00:21:30,245
- She'll get over it,
besides if she doesn't,

462
00:21:30,245 --> 00:21:32,667
you'll be free to marry me.

463
00:21:32,667 --> 00:21:36,656
- Okay, from now on, you're
the other woman in my life.

464
00:21:36,656 --> 00:21:38,373
- [Voiceover] Put her down Jerry Lee.

465
00:21:38,373 --> 00:21:39,675
Oh we got to go.

466
00:21:39,675 --> 00:21:41,584
- Run along now, I've got
some practicing to do.

467
00:21:41,584 --> 00:21:43,323
I'll clean up your magic stuff.

468
00:21:43,323 --> 00:21:44,645
Bye.

469
00:21:44,645 --> 00:21:45,478
- Bye Tom.

470
00:21:56,283 --> 00:21:58,203
- Kennedy would have
won even without Texas.

471
00:21:58,203 --> 00:21:59,440
He didn't need Johnson.

472
00:21:59,440 --> 00:22:01,489
- True, true, but still
it must have been nice

473
00:22:01,489 --> 00:22:02,533
to win Texas.

474
00:22:02,533 --> 00:22:04,432
It probably made him feel real good.

475
00:22:04,432 --> 00:22:05,574
Now what's going on up there?

476
00:22:05,574 --> 00:22:07,493
- [Joel] It's me Joel, I'm cleaning up.

477
00:22:07,493 --> 00:22:10,171
You guys left crunch
berries everywhere up here.

478
00:22:10,171 --> 00:22:12,284
- Ah, that's great, try
to keep quiet will ya?

479
00:22:12,284 --> 00:22:13,424
We're talking here.

480
00:22:13,424 --> 00:22:14,907
- [Joel] Oh great, you
guys just relax while

481
00:22:14,907 --> 00:22:16,347
I clean up your mess.

482
00:22:16,347 --> 00:22:18,320
- Okay great, let us know if we can help.

483
00:22:18,320 --> 00:22:20,592
Anyway Servo, Johnson
Smonson, you can't save it...

484
00:22:20,592 --> 00:22:23,759
Oh, oh, hey, Joel, what are you doing?

485
00:22:24,677 --> 00:22:26,288
Do you have any self control at all?

486
00:22:26,288 --> 00:22:28,262
- [Joel] I fell, I'm
hanging here by one arm.

487
00:22:28,262 --> 00:22:30,021
You guys have to help me.

488
00:22:30,021 --> 00:22:31,697
- Oh Tom, did you hear that?

489
00:22:31,697 --> 00:22:33,296
We have to help Joel.

490
00:22:33,296 --> 00:22:35,249
- Yeah, as a general rule
I don't like being told

491
00:22:35,249 --> 00:22:36,497
what I have to do.

492
00:22:36,497 --> 00:22:38,640
Something about it just gets to me.

493
00:22:38,640 --> 00:22:40,837
- Yeah, well I guess the cat's
on the other foot now huh?

494
00:22:40,837 --> 00:22:41,936
(laughing)

495
00:22:41,936 --> 00:22:43,973
Maybe we should at least
consider helping him though,

496
00:22:43,973 --> 00:22:45,701
he does owe me two space credits.

497
00:22:45,701 --> 00:22:48,603
- Oh I'm willing to consider it.

498
00:22:48,603 --> 00:22:50,181
- [Joel] Come on you guys.

499
00:22:50,181 --> 00:22:53,323
- There may be a few changes
around here though Joel.

500
00:22:53,323 --> 00:22:56,091
For instance, how late
can we stay up tonight?

501
