00:44:20,325 --> 00:44:23,760
Change the oil on a car,
maybe I should chill

1000
00:44:23,760 --> 00:44:26,593
the champagne huh, how about that?

1001
00:44:27,446 --> 00:44:29,958
- [Voiceover] You know booze
is your best drug value.

1002
00:44:29,958 --> 00:44:31,376
- That sweet smell?

1003
00:44:31,376 --> 00:44:32,379
- [Voiceover] Jagermeister honey.

1004
00:44:32,379 --> 00:44:35,419
- It must be the fresh roses.

1005
00:44:35,419 --> 00:44:37,467
- My roses never smell like that.

1006
00:44:37,467 --> 00:44:38,992
- [Voiceover] Than it must be you.

1007
00:44:38,992 --> 00:44:40,784
- It's a women's perfume.

1008
00:44:40,784 --> 00:44:43,525
- Help me make room for these dear.

1009
00:44:43,525 --> 00:44:45,104
In my day it wasn't
candlesticks it was teaspoons.

1010
00:44:45,104 --> 00:44:46,629
- [Voiceover] Shut up.

1011
00:44:46,629 --> 00:44:48,379
- I received no less than 78 of them

1012
00:44:48,379 --> 00:44:50,710
when we were married.

1013
00:44:50,710 --> 00:44:52,421
- [Voiceover] Let's ditch her.

1014
00:44:52,421 --> 00:44:53,584
- When he went back to the main one

1015
00:44:53,584 --> 00:44:54,789
he said he was going to
go right to the office

1016
00:44:54,789 --> 00:44:57,157
and stay there until our wedding.

1017
00:44:57,157 --> 00:44:58,736
I'm sure you'll never
treat your wife like that,

1018
00:44:58,736 --> 00:44:59,718
will you Tom?

1019
00:44:59,718 --> 00:45:01,573
- [Voiceover] You
cleared the room grandma.

1020
00:45:01,573 --> 00:45:03,291
- He isn't here mother.

1021
00:45:03,291 --> 00:45:04,336
- Where is he?

1022
00:45:04,336 --> 00:45:06,939
- I think Meg took him
to look at her dress.

1023
00:45:06,939 --> 00:45:08,240
(screaming)

1024
00:45:08,240 --> 00:45:09,823
- [Voiceover] Next.

1025
00:45:11,397 --> 00:45:13,573
Guess she didn't like it.

1026
00:45:13,573 --> 00:45:14,779
- My wedding dress.

1027
00:45:14,779 --> 00:45:16,592
- [Voiceover] Now it's garbage.

1028
00:45:16,592 --> 00:45:18,053
- What is it?

1029
00:45:18,053 --> 00:45:19,611
What did she find?

1030
00:45:19,611 --> 00:45:20,955
- [Tom] Seaweed.

1031
00:45:20,955 --> 00:45:22,469
- [Voiceover] Well she did
ask for the mermaid cut.

1032
00:45:22,469 --> 00:45:23,867
- [Voiceover] Well we'll
change the bridesmaid

1033
00:45:23,867 --> 00:45:25,284
dresses to green.

1034
00:45:28,688 --> 00:45:30,203
- Tom?

1035
00:45:30,203 --> 00:45:31,227
- Yes, Mrs. Ellis.

1036
00:45:31,227 --> 00:45:35,376
- [Voiceover] No, I wasn't
pretending I was a playmate.

1037
00:45:35,376 --> 00:45:36,613
- I brought you some honey.

1038
00:45:36,613 --> 00:45:37,884
- [Voiceover] Or it might be motor oil.

1039
00:45:37,884 --> 00:45:41,328
- Don't get up, I'll just
put it on the bar here.

1040
00:45:41,328 --> 00:45:44,453
- [Voiceover] Let's wrestle now.

1041
00:45:44,453 --> 00:45:47,643
- I really brought the
honey only as an excuse

1042
00:45:47,643 --> 00:45:50,449
because I knew you were upset.

1043
00:45:50,449 --> 00:45:53,169
Tom, there's nothing
supernatural about what happened

1044
00:45:53,169 --> 00:45:54,864
to Meg's dress?

1045
00:45:54,864 --> 00:45:57,830
There must be a logical explanation.

1046
00:45:57,830 --> 00:45:58,949
- I know, I know.

1047
00:45:58,949 --> 00:46:00,037
- [Voiceover] Maybe she
was rolling sushi on it.

1048
00:46:00,037 --> 00:46:03,099
- Seaweed, it's just
like that Samuel's boy.

1049
00:46:03,099 --> 00:46:05,083
- There have been no recent deaths Tom.

1050
00:46:05,083 --> 00:46:08,581
- [Voiceover] Ha ha, define recent.

1051
00:46:08,581 --> 00:46:10,491
- Any way, I'm sure of one thing.

1052
00:46:10,491 --> 00:46:11,324
- [Voiceover] I'm a turtle.

1053
00:46:11,324 --> 00:46:12,411
- I've had enough of her.

1054
00:46:12,411 --> 00:46:14,085
- Who are you talking about?

1055
00:46:14,085 --> 00:46:18,723
- Oh a friend I used to
have, a girl named Vi.

1056
00:46:18,723 --> 00:46:19,973
- [Voiceover] That I don't have any more.

1057
00:46:19,973 --> 00:46:21,477
- She came over here to the islands.

1058
00:46:21,477 --> 00:46:25,125
- [Voiceover] Fell down off the island.

1059
00:46:25,125 --> 00:46:26,149
- Off the lighthouse.

1060
00:46:26,149 --> 00:46:27,568
- [Voiceover] She died.

1061
00:46:27,568 --> 00:46:29,488
- Well at any rate, she
went back to the mainland.

1062
00:46:29,488 --> 00:46:30,673
- [Voiceover] It's a girl thing.

1063
00:46:30,673 --> 00:46:32,699
- Are you sure that's what happened?

1064
00:46:32,699 --> 00:46:34,224
- What do you mean am I sure?

1065
00:46:34,224 --> 00:46:36,901
- Well maybe she didn't
go back to the mainland.

1066
00:46:36,901 --> 00:46:38,940
Maybe this girl Vi is
still here and is playing

1067
00:46:38,940 --> 00:46:40,123
tricks to get even.

1068
00:46:40,123 --> 00:46:41,445
- [Voiceover] Hey check out Pierre Lupas.

1069
00:46:41,445 --> 00:46:42,629
- [Mrs. Ellis] Now where do
you suppose a woman could hide

1070
00:46:42,629 --> 00:46:43,931
on this island?

1071
00:46:43,931 --> 00:46:45,848
- [Sandy] Who's hiding?

1072
00:46:46,789 --> 00:46:48,187
- Never mind Sandy.

1073
00:46:48,187 --> 00:46:50,299
- [Voiceover] Aye, aye sir.

1074
00:46:50,299 --> 00:46:52,987
- Things will work out, you'll see.

1075
00:46:52,987 --> 00:46:55,654
(evil laughter)

1076
00:46:56,933 --> 00:47:00,100
- [Voiceover] Turn, turn, right, good.

1077
00:47:07,205 --> 00:47:11,372
- [Voiceover] Hello,
hey a kitty (barking).

1078
00:47:13,541 --> 00:47:17,458
- [Voiceover] And Bee
Davis as Mrs. Longstreet.

1079
00:47:18,960 --> 00:47:21,371
- [Sandy] Mrs. Ellis, Mrs. Ellis.

1080
00:47:21,371 --> 00:47:24,038
- [Voiceover] It sure isn't you.

1081
00:47:25,232 --> 00:47:28,059
- Why are people always saying never mind?

1082
00:47:28,059 --> 00:47:30,267
- Because there are some
things that grown ups

1083
00:47:30,267 --> 00:47:32,933
don't want children to know about, Sandy.

1084
00:47:32,933 --> 00:47:35,301
- Those are always the
most interesting things.

1085
00:47:35,301 --> 00:47:37,669
- [Voiceover] And because
you're a bad person Sandy.

1086
00:47:37,669 --> 00:47:38,715
- Why is Tom upset?

1087
00:47:38,715 --> 00:47:39,739
- Never mind.

1088
00:47:39,739 --> 00:47:40,965
- [Voiceover] What is she, Liz Smith?

1089
00:47:40,965 --> 00:47:43,259
- Daddy's looking for
it at the lighthouse.

1090
00:47:43,259 --> 00:47:45,253
He's always hanging around there.

1091
00:47:45,253 --> 00:47:47,760
- The lighthouse is a very
dangerous place, Sandy.

1092
00:47:47,760 --> 00:47:49,296
- [Voiceover] Go play there Sandy.

1093
00:47:49,296 --> 00:47:51,845
- It'll soon be torn down.

1094
00:47:51,845 --> 00:47:53,915
- That doesn't keep
people from going there.

1095
00:47:53,915 --> 00:47:58,000
- But you mustn't go
there Sandy, not ever.

1096
00:47:58,000 --> 00:47:59,952
Run along home now.

1097
00:47:59,952 --> 00:48:03,483
- [Voiceover] Gee you're
a spooky old dame.

1098
00:48:03,483 --> 00:48:06,245
- [Voiceover] Left,
left, oh honey look out.

1099
00:48:06,245 --> 00:48:07,912
- [Voiceover] Clunk.

1100
00:48:08,987 --> 00:48:10,523
- [Voiceover] The dark's
playing a cruel joke on her.

1101
00:48:10,523 --> 00:48:12,690
(barking)

1102
00:48:13,570 --> 00:48:15,056
- [Voiceover] I guess what
I'm saying is I don't want

1103
00:48:15,056 --> 00:48:16,496
to go in there.

1104
00:48:16,496 --> 00:48:18,864
- I'm surprised at you.

1105
00:48:18,864 --> 00:48:20,560
You're being as silly as Tom.

1106
00:48:20,560 --> 00:48:22,811
- [Voiceover] Don't ever say that.

1107
00:48:22,811 --> 00:48:25,531
(barking)

1108
00:48:25,531 --> 00:48:27,781
- All right, I'll go alone.

1109
00:48:34,160 --> 00:48:37,040
- Young lady, young lady?

1110
00:48:37,040 --> 00:48:41,477
- [Voiceover] Young hello
Lady, Mrs. Lady Thing.

1111
00:48:41,477 --> 00:48:42,821
- [Voiceover] Why it's Mrs. Butterworth.

1112
00:48:42,821 --> 00:48:45,477
- I love the perfume you're wearing.

1113
00:48:45,477 --> 00:48:49,227
It's no use, I know
you're in here somewhere.

1114
00:48:50,482 --> 00:48:52,065
I can hear you too.

1115
00:48:53,051 --> 00:48:55,440
Don't you think it's ridiculous to hide?

1116
00:48:55,440 --> 00:48:57,275
- [Voiceover] Just a
second, I'm in the bathroom.

1117
00:48:57,275 --> 00:48:59,141
- There's something I want to say to you.

1118
00:48:59,141 --> 00:49:00,464
- [Voiceover] Grab
something out of the fridge,

1119
00:49:00,464 --> 00:49:01,413
I'll be right down.

1120
00:49:01,413 --> 00:49:04,496
- If you won't, then
I'll go up and find you.

1121
00:49:04,496 --> 00:49:09,200
- [Voiceover] Well better
unpack another body bag.

1122
00:49:09,200 --> 00:49:10,480
- [Voiceover] Is she
wearing a life jacket under

1123
00:49:10,480 --> 00:49:11,313
that sweater?

1124
00:49:11,313 --> 00:49:14,936
- [Voiceover] No she's Mrs. Michelon Man.

1125
00:49:14,936 --> 00:49:16,261
- Listen to me please.

1126
00:49:16,261 --> 00:49:17,371
- [Voiceover] Listen to me please.

1127
00:49:17,371 --> 00:49:19,163
- I don't usually give people advice,

1128
00:49:19,163 --> 00:49:22,000
but Tom is a dear friend
and I want to ask you

1129
00:49:22,000 --> 00:49:23,583
to leave him alone.

1130
00:49:25,179 --> 00:49:27,408
Are you listening to me?

1131
00:49:27,408 --> 00:49:30,373
You might at least have
the politeness to answer.

1132
00:49:30,373 --> 00:49:31,333
(laughing)

1133
00:49:31,333 --> 00:49:33,883
Why that's a nasty laugh you have.

1134
00:49:33,883 --> 00:49:35,419
- [Voiceover] You see I'm dead then.

1135
00:49:35,419 --> 00:49:38,085
- What tricks are you up to now?

1136
00:49:38,085 --> 00:49:39,668
Wait, listen to me.

1137
00:49:41,381 --> 00:49:43,195
- [Voiceover] An aging
Kin Novak re-creates

1138
00:49:43,195 --> 00:49:45,195
this scene from Vertigo.

1139
00:49:46,053 --> 00:49:47,355
- [Voiceover] This place sounds real nice,

1140
00:49:47,355 --> 00:49:49,147
I love what I think you've done with it.

1141
00:49:49,147 --> 00:49:51,835
- You've been frightening
Tom half to death.

1142
00:49:51,835 --> 00:49:55,623
- [Voiceover] What's the
point of being a ghost?

1143
00:49:55,623 --> 00:49:58,363
- I know Meg doesn't concern you,

1144
00:49:58,363 --> 00:49:59,877
but you wouldn't want to
make an innocent person

1145
00:49:59,877 --> 00:50:01,296
suffer, would you?

1146
00:50:01,296 --> 00:50:02,800
- [Voiceover] Well sure,
that's the most fun.

1147
00:50:02,800 --> 00:50:05,029
- I wish you'd speak more clearly.

1148
00:50:05,029 --> 00:50:06,096
- [Voiceover] What do you want, I'm dead?

1149
00:50:06,096 --> 00:50:07,763
My larynx is rotten.

1150
00:50:08,603 --> 00:50:11,247
- You're trying to make
me sorry for you I suppose

1151
00:50:11,247 --> 00:50:13,723
but I can't help thinking
how foolish you are,

1152
00:50:13,723 --> 00:50:15,483
playing this absurd game.

1153
00:50:15,483 --> 00:50:16,549
- [Voiceover] I can't
help thinking how foolish

1154
00:50:16,549 --> 00:50:19,132
she is climbing up that ladder.

1155
00:50:22,545 --> 00:50:23,942
- You have to let me talk to you please.

1156
00:50:23,942 --> 00:50:26,587
- [Voiceover] Hey, I can't
see my house from up here.

1157
00:50:26,587 --> 00:50:30,437
- People all the unhappiness you need to.

1158
00:50:30,437 --> 00:50:31,877
It's time you stopped.

1159
00:50:31,877 --> 00:50:33,499
- [Voiceover] I mean it's fun, but...

1160
00:50:33,499 --> 00:50:36,197
- You don't belong here you know.

1161
00:50:36,197 --> 00:50:37,616
Why don't you leave Tom and Meg alone

1162
00:50:37,616 --> 00:50:38,616
and go back?

1163
00:50:41,115 --> 00:50:42,469
What are you saying?

1164
00:50:42,469 --> 00:50:44,700
- [Voiceover] She's saying
watch that first step.

1165
00:50:44,700 --> 00:50:45,883
- I can't hear you.

1166
00:50:45,883 --> 00:50:49,200
- [Voiceover] On the 50 meter board.

1167
00:50:49,200 --> 00:50:50,801
- [Voiceover] Yeah, the
dog's downstairs checking

1168
00:50:50,801 --> 00:50:52,718
the Want Ads right now.

1169
00:50:53,915 --> 00:50:55,728
- What a fiend you are.

1170
00:50:55,728 --> 00:50:57,765
- [Voiceover] I hate
these one woman shows.

1171
00:50:57,765 --> 00:51:00,069
- You're not fooling me.

1172
00:51:00,069 --> 00:51:02,341
I know exactly what you are.

1173
00:51:02,341 --> 00:51:05,595
- [Voiceover] You're a
superstar, that's what you are.

1174
00:51:05,595 --> 00:51:07,077
(playing piano)

1175
00:51:07,077 --> 00:51:08,755
- [Voiceover] (singing)
Tormented, tormented, tormented,

1176
00:51:08,755 --> 00:51:10,672
tormented, tor-men-ted.

1177
00:51:12,072 --> 00:51:14,813
- [Voiceover] Oh, John Cage.

1178
00:51:14,813 --> 00:51:15,730
- Not fair.

1179
00:51:16,584 --> 00:51:19,923
You're getting the party,
presents, the husband.

1180
00:51:19,923 --> 00:51:21,896
I get nothing.

1181
00:51:21,896 --> 00:51:23,923
- Be nice to me peanut,
in two more days I'll be

1182
00:51:23,923 --> 00:51:25,757
a married woman and you'll miss me.

1183
00:51:25,757 --> 00:51:27,752
- I'll miss Tom more.

1184
00:51:27,752 --> 00:51:28,819
- Sandy.

1185
00:51:28,819 --> 00:51:30,856
- [Voiceover] Oh, what a
beautiful crystal chamber pod.

1186
00:51:30,856 --> 00:51:32,019
- How's my family?

1187
00:51:32,019 --> 00:51:33,117
- [Voiceover] Wrong family.

1188
00:51:33,117 --> 00:51:33,950
- Daddy.

1189
00:51:33,950 --> 00:51:35,791
- Am I too early or too late?

1190
00:51:35,791 --> 00:51:37,584
- I'm so happy you made it in time.

1191
00:51:37,584 --> 00:51:38,821
- You don't think I'd
let my daughter marry

1192
00:51:38,821 --> 00:51:42,139
without her favorite father
being around now do you?

1193
00:51:42,139 --> 00:51:43,813
- Well roll up your sleeves and pitch in,

1194
00:51:43,813 --> 00:51:45,669
the party's right after
tomorrow's rehearsal.

1195
00:51:45,669 --> 00:51:46,811
- Hi honey.

1196
00:51:46,811 --> 00:51:49,061
- [Voiceover] Do I live here?

1197
00:51:49,061 --> 00:51:50,245
- Where's the groom?

1198
00:51:50,245 --> 00:51:51,078
- [Voiceover] Where's my scotch?

1199
00:51:51,078 --> 00:51:52,005
- He's not feeling well.

1200
00:51:52,005 --> 00:51:53,029
- What's the matter with him?

1201
00:51:53,029 --> 00:51:54,480
- [Meg] He's been over working.

1202
00:51:54,480 --> 00:51:55,313
- [Voiceover] Are you a human?

1203
00:51:55,313 --> 00:51:56,944
- At the piano I suppose.

1204
00:51:56,944 --> 00:51:58,587
- Please don't start that again.

1205
00:51:58,587 --> 00:52:00,304
- It's bad enough to accept a musician

1206
00:52:00,304 --> 00:52:02,512
into this family, but a jazz musician

1207
00:52:02,512 --> 00:52:05,136
is asking too damn much.

1208
00:52:05,136 --> 00:52:06,533
- Why don't you go to bed dear?

1209
00:52:06,533 --> 00:52:07,536
You must be tired.

1210
00:52:07,536 --> 00:52:08,955
- [Voiceover] Yeah stay
there for 10 years.

1211
00:52:08,955 --> 00:52:11,600
- What's the matter with a jazz musician?

1212
00:52:11,600 --> 00:52:12,933
- Be still brat.

1213
00:52:14,693 --> 00:52:15,610
- Poor Tom.

1214
00:52:18,053 --> 00:52:19,515
- [Voiceover] I think
there's enough napkins there,

1215
00:52:19,515 --> 00:52:20,348
thank you.

1216
00:52:21,797 --> 00:52:22,981
- [Voiceover] Out for more napkins,

1217
00:52:22,981 --> 00:52:26,299
ran out of napkins, need lots of napkins.

1218
00:52:26,299 --> 00:52:28,411
- [Voiceover] Aw, this is where they make

1219
00:52:28,411 --> 00:52:31,024
Cape Cod potato chips, I
think I'll check it out.

1220
00:52:31,024 --> 00:52:34,320
- [Voiceover] Trick-or-Treat for Unicef.

1221
00:52:34,320 --> 00:52:35,643
- Hi.

1222
00:52:35,643 --> 00:52:38,726
- [Voiceover] She sounds like a seal.

1223
00:52:42,030 --> 00:52:46,624
- [Voiceover] Well she's like
the Gordon's Fishermen babies.

1224
00:52:46,624 --> 00:52:48,006
(banging)

1225
00:52:48,006 --> 00:52:51,423
- [Voiceover] Okay, I'll come back later.

1226
00:52:53,756 --> 00:52:55,256
Stupid hat tricks.

1227
00:53:00,188 --> 00:53:02,886
Hey, two years sobriety.

1228
00:53:02,886 --> 00:53:07,053
My name is Vi, I'm a schnauzer,
I belong to Tom Stewart.

1229
00:53:10,440 --> 00:53:12,315
- [Voiceover] What do you know, Vi's fixed

1230
00:53:12,315 --> 00:53:14,732
the windows and the railings.

1231
00:53:20,795 --> 00:53:23,212
- [Voiceover] You call a cab?

1232
00:53:24,805 --> 00:53:27,035
- You live here kid?

1233
00:53:27,035 --> 00:53:28,336
- [Voiceover] Just move away.

1234
00:53:28,336 --> 00:53:30,640
Don't make me use this thing.

1235
00:53:30,640 --> 00:53:33,211
- Can't you hear or something,
I asked if you lived here?

1236
00:53:33,211 --> 00:53:34,225
- In the lighthouse?

1237
00:53:34,225 --> 00:53:35,892
- No, on the island?

1238
00:53:37,158 --> 00:53:38,550
On the island?

1239
00:53:38,550 --> 00:53:39,564
- [Voiceover] Hey I'm just a little kid.

1240
00:53:39,564 --> 00:53:42,124
- Look kid I really don't care.

1241
00:53:42,124 --> 00:53:43,329
- [Voiceover] I'm a New York method actor,

1242
00:53:43,329 --> 00:53:44,278
give me a break.

1243
00:53:44,278 --> 00:53:45,910
- I'm looking for a
guy called Tom Stewart.

